#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bd-shuffle-lane -- an ADVISORY, SEED-RECORDED shuffle lane that finds order
dependencies between test files. It is a SECOND lane; it never replaces or
edits the CLAUDE.md A5 canonical full-suite command.

    venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --install     # once per host
    venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane               # run the lane
    venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --seed 4126   # replay a finding
    venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --control     # positive control
    venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --selftest    # toolchain convention

WHY THIS EXISTS. `--dist loadfile` hands one FILE to whichever worker is free,
so the neighbour set of any given file differs from run to run and a
cross-file leak surfaces only by luck. Three such leaks are already filed --
backlog rows 491, 516 and 610 -- and row 610's own note records the giveaway
shape: the file "passes in isolation" and fails beside a particular neighbour.
Nothing in this tree deliberately varies test ORDER, so nothing looks for that
class on purpose. This lane does.

WHY `-p no:randomly` IN THE A5 COMMAND IS NOT A CONTRADICTION, and why it must
stay. MEASURED at v3.66.1451: pytest-randomly was not installed at all, so that
token guarded a plugin that did not exist and had never done anything. It is
kept, byte for byte, because the canonical lane's value is that it is
DETERMINISTIC -- A5 says a different plugin is a different experiment and
cannot authorize merge. Now that the plugin can exist on a host, that token is
what keeps the canonical lane the same experiment it has always been. This tool
does not read, edit or reformat CLAUDE.md; a tracked gate
(tests/test_v3_66_1452_a_shuffle_lane_finds_order_dependencies.py) pins the
canonical line's exact bytes so that no future change to this lane can drift
it.

## THE CONTAINMENT PROBLEM, AND WHY THE PLUGIN LIVES IN A PRIVATE DIRECTORY

pytest auto-loads a plugin from its setuptools entry point. Installing
pytest-randomly into the repository venv would therefore turn shuffling ON for
EVERY pytest invocation that does not pass `-p no:randomly` -- which includes
the affected-band lane, `bd-precut --gate`, every ci.yml gate-suite shard, and
most of the sub-pytest children the tracked tests spawn. In a tree with live
order dependencies that converts merge evidence into noise. So the plugin is
declared in `requirements-shuffle.txt`, which NO default installer converges
(deploy.sh, cloud-setup.sh, provision_test_host.sh and ci.yml all name their
manifests explicitly; none globs `requirements*.txt`), and `--install` puts it
in a private directory that only this tool places on PYTHONPATH.

`--install` passes `--no-deps` deliberately. Without it a `pip install --target`
re-resolves pytest ITSELF into the target directory and PYTHONPATH then shadows
the venv's interpreter-blessed pytest with a second copy -- a second changed
variable in an experiment whose whole point is to change exactly one. The
install verifies afterwards that the target holds nothing but pytest_randomly,
and refuses if it does not.

## ADVISORY -- AND HOW A MAINTAINER PROMOTES IT TO BLOCKING

"Advisory" here is STRUCTURAL, not a softened exit code. A FINDINGS verdict
exits 3 and an unmeasurable one exits 4, because a refusal that reports instead
of refusing is the failure this repository has hit repeatedly. What makes the
lane advisory is that NOTHING ON THE MERGE PATH INVOKES IT: it is absent from
`toolchain/bin/bd-precut`, from `toolchain/bin/bd-band-derive`, from
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` and from `scripts/deploy.sh`, and the tracked gate
asserts that absence mechanically. A finding is therefore information for
triage, and cannot fail anybody's PR until a human decides it should.

TO PROMOTE IT TO BLOCKING, once its findings are triaged and the tree is clean
under shuffle, a maintainer does exactly three things:

  1. provision the plugin wherever the blocking lane will run -- for CI that is
     an `--install` step on the chosen shard, next to the existing conditional
     install steps in ci.yml;
  2. invoke this tool from that lane, e.g. add a shard that runs
     `venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --seed <pinned>` (pin the
     seed, or the gate's subject changes every run and a red is unreproducible);
  3. DELETE `test_the_lane_is_not_wired_into_any_merge_gate` from
     tests/test_v3_66_1452_a_shuffle_lane_finds_order_dependencies.py, which
     exists precisely so that promotion is a deliberate, reviewed edit rather
     than something that happens by accident.

Do not promote it by making findings exit 0. That is the fail-open shape.

## VERDICTS AND EXIT CODES

    0  PASS      the shuffled run was green over a nonzero collected denominator
    3  FINDINGS  the shuffled run failed; the seed and a replay command are printed
    4  UNKNOWN   the lane could not measure (plugin absent, zero collected,
                 the seed was not echoed back, no JUnit record). A2: UNKNOWN is
                 a failing third state, never permission.
    2  usage / internal error

A ZERO COLLECTED DENOMINATOR IS UNKNOWN, NOT OK. A shuffle lane that collects
nothing has judged nothing, and reporting that as a clean run is the exact
"gate that cannot see its subject" defect CLAUDE.md A7 forbids. The lane takes
its expected denominator from pytest's own `collected N items` line and its
executed denominator from the JUnit record, keeps both, and refuses when either
is absent or zero.

## THE SEED IS ALWAYS CHOSEN BY THIS TOOL, NEVER BY THE PLUGIN

The wrapper picks the seed (or takes `--seed`), passes it explicitly as
`--randomly-seed=N`, then PARSES pytest's own `Using --randomly-seed=N` header
and asserts it matches. That is the seam proof: it distinguishes "the plugin
loaded and honoured the seed" from "the plugin was silently absent and the run
was in file order" -- two states with the same exit code when the run happens
to pass. Under `-n 24` it doubles as evidence the seed reached the workers
rather than each worker choosing its own, which is what makes a finding
replayable at all.

`--randomly-dont-reset-seed` is passed deliberately. pytest-randomly otherwise
also reseeds `random.seed()` before every test, which is a SECOND variable; the
subject of this lane is ORDER, and a finding that cannot be attributed to order
is not a finding about order.

## KNOWN LIMITATION, STATED RATHER THAN SOLVED

PYTHONPATH is inherited by child processes, so the ~26 tracked test files that
spawn their own sub-pytest DO gain the plugin in that child. The ones that pass
`-p no:randomly` (which is most of them, and which was until now a no-op) stay
deterministic -- that is the token finally doing its job. An unguarded inner run
will shuffle with its own self-chosen seed, which this tool does not record. So
a finding whose failing test spawns a sub-pytest must be replayed as a PAIR at
the recorded outer seed before causation is claimed.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
import pathlib
import random
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET

EXIT_PASS = 0
EXIT_USAGE = 2
EXIT_FINDINGS = 3
EXIT_UNKNOWN = 4

MANIFEST = "requirements-shuffle.txt"
CONTROL_DIR = os.path.join("tests", "fixtures", "shuffle_control")
CONTROL_ALPHA = "order_probe_alpha.py"
CONTROL_BETA = "order_probe_beta.py"
CONTROL_MARKER = "BD-SHUFFLE-CONTROL: order dependency observed"
EXPECT_VAR = "BD_SHUFFLE_CONTROL_EXPECT"
TOKEN_VAR = "BD_SHUFFLE_CONTROL_TOKEN"

_SEED_ECHO = re.compile(r"^Using --randomly-seed=(\d+)\s*$", re.M)
_COLLECTED = re.compile(r"^collected (\d+) items?", re.M)
_XDIST_COLLECTED = re.compile(r"^\d+ workers \[(\d+) items?\]", re.M)


def _utc() -> str:
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(
        "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def _repo_root(explicit: "str | None") -> str:
    """The repository this lane judges. Never guessed from cwd alone."""
    if explicit:
        return os.path.abspath(explicit)
    here = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(
        os.path.realpath(__file__))))
    return here


def default_plugin_dir() -> str:
    """Outside the repository, on purpose.

    A plugin directory inside the tree would show up as untracked state in
    every `git status` the lifecycle inspects, and could be swept by a cleanup
    that does not know it is load-bearing. The XDG state path is the same
    convention `toolchain/bin/bd-sbcap` already uses.
    """
    env = os.environ.get("BD_SHUFFLE_PLUGIN_DIR")
    if env:
        return os.path.abspath(env)
    state = os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or os.path.join(
        os.path.expanduser("~"), ".local", "state")
    return os.path.join(state, "bulkdownloader", "shuffle-lane", "plugins")


def _git(root: str, *args: str) -> str:
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", root, *args],
                              capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""
    return done.stdout.strip() if done.returncode == 0 else ""


def plugin_state(plugin_dir: str, python: str) -> dict:
    """RUNTIME evidence that the plugin is importable from `plugin_dir`.

    Deliberately an import in a real child process rather than a directory
    listing: CLAUDE.md A7 says source reading is not runtime evidence, and a
    half-extracted `--target` install lists a directory that does not import.
    """
    if not os.path.isdir(plugin_dir):
        return {"available": False, "why": "plugin directory does not exist",
                "dir": plugin_dir, "version": None}
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["PYTHONPATH"] = plugin_dir + os.pathsep + env.get("PYTHONPATH", "")
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(
            [python, "-c",
             "import pytest_randomly, sys;"
             "from importlib.metadata import version, PackageNotFoundError;"
             "\ntry: v = version('pytest-randomly')"
             "\nexcept PackageNotFoundError: v = 'installed-without-metadata'"
             "\nsys.stdout.write(v)"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120, env=env)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        return {"available": False, "why": "import probe could not run: %s" % exc,
                "dir": plugin_dir, "version": None}
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return {"available": False,
                "why": "pytest_randomly is not importable from the plugin "
                       "directory: %s" % (done.stderr.strip()[-300:] or "no stderr"),
                "dir": plugin_dir, "version": None}
    return {"available": True, "why": "", "dir": plugin_dir,
            "version": done.stdout.strip()}


def install(root: str, plugin_dir: str, python: str) -> int:
    """Provision the private plugin directory from requirements-shuffle.txt."""
    manifest = os.path.join(root, MANIFEST)
    if not os.path.isfile(manifest):
        print("UNKNOWN  %s is missing -- nothing declares what to install"
              % MANIFEST)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    os.makedirs(plugin_dir, exist_ok=True)
    cmd = [python, "-m", "pip", "install", "--target", plugin_dir,
           "--no-deps", "--upgrade", "-r", manifest]
    print("installing: %s" % " ".join(cmd))
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(cmd, timeout=900)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        print("UNKNOWN  pip could not run: %s" % exc)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    if done.returncode != 0:
        print("UNKNOWN  pip exited %d -- the plugin directory is not provisioned"
              % done.returncode)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    # THE --no-deps PROOF. A target install that dragged pytest in would make
    # PYTHONPATH shadow the venv's pytest, and the lane would then be running a
    # different interpreter's test framework while claiming to differ from the
    # canonical command by one plugin.
    stray = sorted(n for n in os.listdir(plugin_dir)
                   if not n.startswith("pytest_randomly")
                   and not n.startswith("__pycache__")
                   and not n.endswith(".pth"))
    if stray:
        print("UNKNOWN  the plugin directory holds more than pytest_randomly, "
              "so PYTHONPATH would shadow the venv: %s" % ", ".join(stray))
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    state = plugin_state(plugin_dir, python)
    if not state["available"]:
        print("UNKNOWN  installed, but %s" % state["why"])
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    print("OK  pytest-randomly %s in %s" % (state["version"], plugin_dir))
    return EXIT_PASS


def _run_pytest(python: str, cwd: str, args: list, plugin_dir: str,
                extra_env: "dict | None" = None,
                pop_env: "tuple | None" = None,
                timeout: int = 7200) -> dict:
    """One real pytest run with the plugin on PYTHONPATH. Returns raw evidence."""
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.pop("BD_INSTALL_DIR", None)          # A5: pop, never merely omit.
    for name in (pop_env or ()):             # same discipline, caller's names.
        env.pop(name, None)
    env["BD_DISABLE_KEEPALIVE"] = "1"
    env["PYTHONUNBUFFERED"] = "1"
    env["PYTHONPATH"] = plugin_dir + os.pathsep + env.get("PYTHONPATH", "")
    if extra_env:
        env.update(extra_env)
    cmd = [python, "-m", "pytest", *args]
    started = _utc()
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True,
                              timeout=timeout, env=env)
        out, rc, timed_out = done.stdout + done.stderr, done.returncode, False
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:
        out = (exc.stdout or "") + (exc.stderr or "")
        if isinstance(out, bytes):
            out = out.decode("utf-8", "replace")
        rc, timed_out = None, True
    return {"cmd": cmd, "cmd_digest": hashlib.sha256(
                (" ".join(cmd)).encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(),
            "rc": rc, "timed_out": timed_out, "output": out,
            "started": started, "ended": _utc()}


def _echoed_seed(output: str) -> "int | None":
    m = _SEED_ECHO.search(output)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None


def _collected(output: str) -> "int | None":
    m = _COLLECTED.search(output)
    if m:
        return int(m.group(1))
    m = _XDIST_COLLECTED.search(output)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None


def _junit_counts(path: str) -> "dict | None":
    """Executed denominator, independent of the terminal summary text."""
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        return None
    try:
        root = ET.parse(path).getroot()
    except ET.ParseError:
        return None
    suites = [root] if root.tag == "testsuite" else list(root)
    total = {"tests": 0, "failures": 0, "errors": 0, "skipped": 0}
    for s in suites:
        for k in total:
            try:
                total[k] += int(s.get(k, "0"))
            except (TypeError, ValueError):
                return None
    return total


def _write_evidence(path: str, record: dict) -> None:
    """temp + os.replace: a reader must never catch a fragment (row 222)."""
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        json.dump(record, fh, indent=2, sort_keys=True)
        fh.flush()
        os.fsync(fh.fileno())
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def _prove_writable(directory: str) -> "str | None":
    """A7: an action with a side effect proves its evidence record is writable
    BEFORE acting, not after the run it was supposed to record."""
    try:
        os.makedirs(directory, exist_ok=True)
        probe = os.path.join(directory, ".bd-shuffle-lane-writable")
        with open(probe, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(_utc())
        os.unlink(probe)
    except OSError as exc:
        return "evidence directory %s is not writable: %s" % (directory, exc)
    return None


def lane(root: str, plugin_dir: str, python: str, targets: list, seed: "int|None",
         workers: int, evidence_dir: str, timeout: int, per_test_timeout: int) -> int:
    """The lane itself: the canonical shape, shuffled, with a recorded seed."""
    state = plugin_state(plugin_dir, python)
    if not state["available"]:
        print("UNKNOWN  %s" % state["why"])
        print("REMEDY   venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --install"
              "  (declares from %s into %s)" % (MANIFEST, plugin_dir))
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    problem = _prove_writable(evidence_dir)
    if problem:
        print("UNKNOWN  %s" % problem)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    if seed is None:
        seed = random.SystemRandom().randrange(0, 2 ** 32)
    stamp = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ")
    junit = os.path.join(evidence_dir, "shuffle-%s-seed%d.xml" % (stamp, seed))
    logpath = os.path.join(evidence_dir, "shuffle-%s-seed%d.log" % (stamp, seed))
    record_path = os.path.join(evidence_dir, "shuffle-%s-seed%d.json" % (stamp, seed))

    # THE CANONICAL SHAPE, differing from CLAUDE.md A5 in exactly one token:
    # `-p no:randomly` becomes `-p randomly` plus this lane's own seed control.
    args = [*targets, "-n", str(workers), "--dist", "loadfile",
            "--timeout=%d" % per_test_timeout, "--timeout-method=signal",
            "--max-worker-restart=0",
            "-p", "randomly", "--randomly-seed=%d" % seed,
            "--randomly-dont-reset-seed",
            "--junitxml=%s" % junit]

    replay = ("venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --seed %d "
              "-n %d %s" % (seed, workers, " ".join(targets)))
    print("seed     %d" % seed)
    print("replay   %s" % replay)
    print("evidence %s" % record_path)

    run = _run_pytest(python, root, args, plugin_dir, timeout=timeout)
    try:
        with open(logpath, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(run["output"])
    except OSError as exc:
        print("UNKNOWN  the run happened but its log could not be written: %s" % exc)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    echoed = _echoed_seed(run["output"])
    expected = _collected(run["output"])
    executed = _junit_counts(junit)

    record = {
        "tool": "bd-shuffle-lane", "verdict": None, "seed": seed,
        "seed_echoed_by_pytest": echoed, "replay_command": replay,
        "host": os.uname().nodename, "repo": root,
        "git_head": _git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD"),
        "git_tree": _git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD^{tree}"),
        "git_branch": _git(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD"),
        "git_dirty": _git(root, "status", "--porcelain"),
        "python": python, "plugin_dir": plugin_dir,
        "plugin_version": state["version"],
        "targets": targets, "workers": workers,
        "command": run["cmd"], "command_digest": run["cmd_digest"],
        "raw_returncode": run["rc"], "timed_out": run["timed_out"],
        "expected_collected": expected, "junit_counts": executed,
        "junit_path": junit, "log_path": logpath,
        "started_utc": run["started"], "ended_utc": run["ended"],
        "log_sha256": hashlib.sha256(run["output"].encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(),
        "advisory": True,
        "advisory_note": "nothing on the merge path invokes this tool; see the "
                         "module docstring for the promotion recipe",
    }

    def finish(verdict: str, code: int, why: str) -> int:
        record["verdict"] = verdict
        record["why"] = why
        _write_evidence(record_path, record)
        # An ATOMIC COMPLETION MARKER, written last and only on a finished run.
        _write_evidence(record_path + ".complete",
                        {"verdict": verdict, "seed": seed, "at": _utc()})
        print("%-8s %s" % (verdict, why))
        if verdict == "FINDINGS":
            print("REPLAY THIS FINDING:  %s" % replay)
        return code

    if run["timed_out"]:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "the run exceeded --lane-timeout=%ds; a truncated run has "
                      "no denominator" % timeout)
    if echoed is None:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "pytest never printed 'Using --randomly-seed=' -- the "
                      "plugin did not load, so this run was NOT shuffled and a "
                      "green result would mean nothing")
    if echoed != seed:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "asked for seed %d, pytest reports %d -- the finding "
                      "would not be replayable" % (seed, echoed))
    if not expected:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "pytest reported no collected denominator; a lane that "
                      "collected nothing has judged nothing")
    if executed is None:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "no readable JUnit record at %s, so the executed "
                      "denominator is unknown" % junit)
    if executed["tests"] == 0:
        return finish("UNKNOWN", EXIT_UNKNOWN,
                      "collected %d but executed 0 -- nothing ran" % expected)
    if run["rc"] != 0:
        return finish("FINDINGS", EXIT_FINDINGS,
                      "shuffled run rc=%s over %d collected / %d executed: "
                      "%d failure(s), %d error(s)"
                      % (run["rc"], expected, executed["tests"],
                         executed["failures"], executed["errors"]))
    return finish("PASS", EXIT_PASS,
                  "shuffled green at seed %d over %d collected / %d executed"
                  % (seed, expected, executed["tests"]))


def materialize_control(root: str, dest: str) -> "list | None":
    """Copy the tracked control pair into `dest` under collectable names.

    The tracked files are NOT named test_*.py so the real suite never collects
    them; a directory-level shuffled run needs names the collector accepts, and
    copying is what keeps both facts true at once.
    """
    src = os.path.join(root, CONTROL_DIR)
    pairs = [(CONTROL_ALPHA, "test_probe_alpha.py"),
             (CONTROL_BETA, "test_probe_beta.py")]
    out = []
    for name, target in pairs:
        origin = os.path.join(src, name)
        if not os.path.isfile(origin):
            return None
        shutil.copy2(origin, os.path.join(dest, target))
        out.append(target)
    return out


def control(root: str, plugin_dir: str, python: str, lo: int, hi: int) -> int:
    """THE POSITIVE CONTROL. A lane that cannot fail is not a lane.

    Plants a known order dependency, shuffles it across a searched seed range,
    and requires BOTH classes to be non-empty over a nonzero denominator:

      * at least one seed where the pair FAILS -- proof the lane can fail, and
        proof it fails for the INTENDED reason (the control's own distinctive
        diagnostic must appear, not a collection error or an import failure);
      * at least one seed where the pair PASSES -- the negative control. Without
        it, a lane broken so that everything fails would look like a lane that
        works.

    It does NOT pin a seed-to-order mapping. That mapping is pytest-randomly's
    private business and may change with the plugin; what must hold is that the
    lane REACHES both orders, which is a property of shuffling rather than of a
    particular implementation.

    Finally it REPLAYS the failing seed and requires the identical verdict. A
    finding nobody can reproduce is not a finding.
    """
    state = plugin_state(plugin_dir, python)
    if not state["available"]:
        print("UNKNOWN  %s" % state["why"])
        print("REMEDY   venv/bin/python toolchain/bin/bd-shuffle-lane --install")
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    if hi <= lo:
        print("UNKNOWN  empty seed range %d..%d -- nothing would be searched"
              % (lo, hi))
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    token = "bd-shuffle-control-%s" % os.urandom(8).hex()
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="bd-shuffle-control-") as work:
        if materialize_control(root, work) is None:
            print("UNKNOWN  the tracked control pair is missing under %s"
                  % CONTROL_DIR)
            return EXIT_UNKNOWN

        # A FRESH token per invocation, and TOKEN_VAR popped from the CHILD's
        # environment -- which is where it matters, and which merely declining
        # to set it does not achieve (CLAUDE.md A7). An inherited token would
        # let the consumer probe pass in either order, and the control would
        # then certify a lane that cannot fail.
        extra = {EXPECT_VAR: token}

        failing, passing, broken = [], [], []
        for seed in range(lo, hi):
            args = [work, "-p", "randomly", "--randomly-seed=%d" % seed,
                    "--randomly-dont-reset-seed", "-p", "no:cacheprovider",
                    "--timeout=60", "--timeout-method=signal"]
            run = _run_pytest(python, work, args, plugin_dir,
                              extra_env=dict(extra), pop_env=(TOKEN_VAR,),
                              timeout=300)
            if _echoed_seed(run["output"]) != seed:
                broken.append((seed, "seed not echoed"))
                continue
            if _collected(run["output"]) != 2:
                broken.append((seed, "collected %r, expected exactly the two "
                                     "control probes" % _collected(run["output"])))
                continue
            if run["rc"] == 0:
                passing.append(seed)
            elif CONTROL_MARKER in run["output"]:
                failing.append(seed)
            else:
                broken.append((seed, "rc=%s without the control's own "
                                     "diagnostic" % run["rc"]))

        searched = hi - lo
        print("searched %d seed(s) in [%d,%d)" % (searched, lo, hi))
        print("failing  %s" % (failing[:8] or "NONE"))
        print("passing  %s" % (passing[:8] or "NONE"))
        if broken:
            print("broken   %s" % broken[:8])
            print("UNKNOWN  %d of %d searched seeds produced neither a clean "
                  "pass nor the control's own failure -- the control cannot "
                  "grade the lane" % (len(broken), searched))
            return EXIT_UNKNOWN
        if not failing:
            print("UNKNOWN  no seed in [%d,%d) put the consumer probe first, so "
                  "this run does not show the lane CAN fail. Widen the range."
                  % (lo, hi))
            return EXIT_UNKNOWN
        if not passing:
            print("UNKNOWN  every searched seed failed, so the control cannot "
                  "distinguish an order-sensitive lane from a broken one")
            return EXIT_UNKNOWN

        # REPLAY: the same seed must reproduce the same verdict, or a recorded
        # seed buys nothing.
        seed = failing[0]
        args = [work, "-p", "randomly", "--randomly-seed=%d" % seed,
                "--randomly-dont-reset-seed", "-p", "no:cacheprovider",
                "--timeout=60", "--timeout-method=signal"]
        again = _run_pytest(python, work, args, plugin_dir,
                            extra_env=dict(extra), pop_env=(TOKEN_VAR,),
                            timeout=300)
        if again["rc"] == 0 or CONTROL_MARKER not in again["output"]:
            print("UNKNOWN  replaying seed %d did not reproduce the finding, so "
                  "the recorded seed is not a replay handle" % seed)
            return EXIT_UNKNOWN

    print("PASS     the lane FAILS on a planted order dependency (seed %d, "
          "replayed), PASSES on the benign order (seed %d), over %d searched "
          "seeds" % (seed, passing[0], searched))
    return EXIT_PASS


def selftest() -> int:
    """Toolchain-convention selftest. Deliberately DOES NOT need the plugin.

    `bd-tool-lint --gate` runs this on hosts that have never provisioned the
    lane, so a selftest that required pytest-randomly would report FAIL for an
    environmental reason -- the over-sensitive direction CLAUDE.md A7 counts as
    equal to a false clean. What it proves instead is the part that must hold
    everywhere: the refusal paths refuse, and they refuse DISTINCTLY.
    """
    root = _repo_root(None)
    checks = []

    def check(name: str, ok: bool, detail: str = "") -> None:
        checks.append((name, ok, detail))
        print("%s  %s%s" % ("PASS" if ok else "FAIL", name,
                            ("  -- " + detail) if detail and not ok else ""))

    check("control pair is tracked and is NOT named test_*.py",
          all(os.path.isfile(os.path.join(root, CONTROL_DIR, n))
              for n in (CONTROL_ALPHA, CONTROL_BETA))
          and not any(n.startswith("test") for n in (CONTROL_ALPHA, CONTROL_BETA)),
          "the control pair must exist and must not pollute `pytest tests/`")

    check("the shuffle manifest exists",
          os.path.isfile(os.path.join(root, MANIFEST)), MANIFEST)

    # THE REFUSAL PATH, exercised for real rather than read: an empty plugin
    # directory must return UNKNOWN and name the remedy, not report OK.
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="bd-shuffle-selftest-") as empty:
        state = plugin_state(empty, sys.executable)
        check("an empty plugin directory is UNAVAILABLE, not silently fine",
              state["available"] is False and bool(state["why"]),
              "state=%r" % state)

    check("a missing plugin directory is UNAVAILABLE",
          plugin_state(os.path.join(root, "no-such-plugin-dir-%s"
                                    % os.urandom(4).hex()),
                       sys.executable)["available"] is False)

    # The denominator readers must be honest about absence: this is the
    # zero-denominator refusal the lane is built on.
    check("a run with no collected line yields no denominator",
          _collected("nothing at all here") is None)
    check("a collected line is read exactly",
          _collected("collected 41 items\n") == 41)
    check("an xdist collected line is read exactly",
          _collected("24 workers [1234 items]\n") == 1234)
    check("a missing seed echo is None, never 0",
          _echoed_seed("no header here") is None)
    check("the seed echo is read exactly",
          _echoed_seed("Using --randomly-seed=99\n") == 99)
    check("a missing JUnit file yields None, not a zero count",
          _junit_counts(os.path.join(root, "no-such-junit-%s.xml"
                                     % os.urandom(4).hex())) is None)

    ok = all(c[1] for c in checks)
    print("SELFTEST PASS" if ok else "SELFTEST FAIL")
    return EXIT_PASS if ok else 1


def main(argv=None) -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="bd-shuffle-lane",
        description="ADVISORY shuffle lane -- finds order dependencies between "
                    "test files. Never edits or replaces the CLAUDE.md A5 "
                    "canonical full-suite command.")
    ap.add_argument("targets", nargs="*", default=None,
                    help="pytest targets (default: tests/)")
    ap.add_argument("--work", default=None, help="repository root")
    ap.add_argument("--plugin-dir", default=None,
                    help="private pytest-randomly directory (default: "
                         "$BD_SHUFFLE_PLUGIN_DIR or the XDG state path)")
    ap.add_argument("--python", default=sys.executable,
                    help="interpreter (default: the one running this tool)")
    ap.add_argument("--install", action="store_true",
                    help="provision the private plugin directory and exit")
    ap.add_argument("--control", action="store_true",
                    help="run the positive control and exit")
    ap.add_argument("--selftest", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--seed", type=int, default=None,
                    help="replay an exact seed instead of choosing one")
    ap.add_argument("--seed-range", default="0:24",
                    help="LO:HI seed range searched by --control")
    ap.add_argument("-n", "--workers", type=int, default=24,
                    help="xdist workers (default 24, the canonical shape)")
    ap.add_argument("--evidence-dir", default=None,
                    help="where the JSON/JUnit/log record is written")
    ap.add_argument("--lane-timeout", type=int, default=7200,
                    help="whole-run wall-clock cap in seconds")
    ap.add_argument("--per-test-timeout", type=int, default=240,
                    help="pytest-timeout per item (default 240, canonical)")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)

    if a.selftest:
        return selftest()

    root = _repo_root(a.work)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root, "tests")):
        print("UNKNOWN  %s does not look like the repository (no tests/)" % root)
        return EXIT_UNKNOWN
    plugin_dir = os.path.abspath(a.plugin_dir) if a.plugin_dir else default_plugin_dir()

    if a.install:
        return install(root, plugin_dir, a.python)

    if a.control:
        try:
            lo_s, hi_s = a.seed_range.split(":", 1)
            lo, hi = int(lo_s), int(hi_s)
        except ValueError:
            print("usage: --seed-range LO:HI")
            return EXIT_USAGE
        return control(root, plugin_dir, a.python, lo, hi)

    targets = a.targets or ["tests/"]
    evidence = a.evidence_dir or os.path.join(
        pathlib.Path.home(), ".local", "state", "bulkdownloader",
        "shuffle-lane", "runs")
    return lane(root, plugin_dir, a.python, targets, a.seed, a.workers,
                evidence, a.lane_timeout, a.per_test_timeout)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
